{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For YHWH will turn again to rejoice over you for good, as He rejoiced over your fathers.</b> It is possible that this verse alludes to the return of the King with the Bride in the time of redemption, and the reading of the verse is thus: 'for YHWH will turn again for good, to rejoice over you, as He rejoiced over your fathers.' And the explanation of the matter is that the honored Name will leave you surplus in all the work of your hands — that is, He will give you an advantage of goodness when the King returns to the kingship, and then He will rejoice over you as He rejoiced over your fathers. And if you ask: when will He return? Therefore He mentioned after it כי תשמע, כי תשוב — in the manner of the verse (Malachi 3:7): שובו אלי ואשובה אליכם. And it teaches us that the matter depends on repentance. And the explanation of ואשובה אליכם — 'and I shall return' with a final Heh — for your need. And understand this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:21.626085092Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}